{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  Solo Therapy — FAQPage structured data for /pages/faqs
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  NOTE: 00-ALL-SCHEMA-single-file.liquid supersedes this file. Use that
  instead unless you specifically want the schema split across files.

  WHERE THIS GOES
    1. Snippets → Add a new snippet → name it exactly: st-faq-schema
    2. Paste this file in, Save.
    3. In layout/theme.liquid, inside the <head>, add:

           {% if page.handle == 'faqs' %}{% render 'st-faq-schema' %}{% endif %}

       (If you added 02-organization-and-breadcrumbs.liquid, put this line
       directly beneath that one.)

  IMPORTANT
    The two Q&As below are transcribed verbatim from your live FAQ page.
    Google requires that FAQ schema match the visible page text exactly.
    If you edit the FAQ page copy, edit this file to match — otherwise the
    markup becomes invalid.

  WORTH KNOWING
    Google now shows FAQ rich results mainly for authoritative health and
    government sites, so treat this as correctness-and-completeness work
    rather than a guaranteed SERP feature. It still helps AI assistants and
    Shopify's own agentic-commerce endpoints answer questions about you
    accurately — and those endpoints are already live on your store.

    Your FAQ page has only two questions totalling ~550 characters. Adding
    5–8 more real questions (Do you ship internationally? Are the herbs
    organic? How should I store dried herbs? Do you offer wholesale?) would
    do more for you than the markup itself.
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does it take to ship?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Your items are shipped within 24 hours of placing your order. Currently, we offer standard shipping which can take 5-7 business days once shipped, and expedited shipping which takes 2-4 business days to deliver."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is your return policy?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Your experience is so important to us. We offer 30-day returns for a full refund, no questions asked. All we ask is that you pay for shipping and handling to return your item. Once we receive your item, your refund should show up on your debit or credit card within 2-3 days."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>
